# Intent: Telling from the unit's own pantry with no host (owner decisions 25 and 26; screens UX17; core SF92 and device SF93). The tool self.pantry.tell (kind joke, riddle or trivia, and a language) starts a session of the question games in which the unit plays the host's part: a joke or riddle shows its words and a Reveal button (the punchline or answer shows under the words and stays until Next); trivia shows the question and two or three answer tiles (the right answer shuffled among the record's wrong ones), judges the tap itself, shows the verdict for 1.2 s with a sound, keeps the score over 5 questions and ends on the shared game-over screen (won with at least half right; Play again starts another round). Each record shown is reported to the pantry as told (the heard list is written in batches). A session with no shelf, or none that has an unheard record in the language, refuses in words; one that runs out of records ends with a notice. A local session never times out waiting for a host. The screens, touch rules, quiet, lock and update rules are the question games' (SF88): this patch adds only the unit-side host.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_qa_game.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: with a pantry shelf installed (SF93 check), self.pantry.tell joke shows a setup with Reveal, Reveal shows the punchline, Next shows another joke and self.pantry.heard lists the tellings; trivia shows tiles, a tap shows right or wrong with a sound and the score counts, the fifth question ends on the game-over screen; with no shelf the call refuses with a sentence that says to ask the host to fill the pantry.
# Kconfig: none (compiled with MAIPAI_GAMES; the pantry calls are stubs without MAIPAI_PANTRY)
# Memory cost: nothing beyond the question games' (screen.qa_games): the session state grows by about 360 bytes in PSRAM (one pantry record, the answer tiles and the random state); no internal RAM.

